{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: cut the structural round-trips in the MCP read/write surface, measured during the 2026-08-19 backlog settlement. The board rows carry complete event ids but not the context to act on them, so the two routine workflows are multi-trip today: triaging 34 reported lanes honestly would have taken ~34 inspect calls because settled-vs-in-flight is decided by three fields (report body.status, reported head, latest review verdict) that only inspect returns; and filing any request needs a live-artifact basis that no MCP query can answer, forcing a full /v0/status fetch (12MB) that defeats the bounded transport (adda28c8). Write results compound it: a state result returns the record and commit but no fold ruling, so every batch needs a post-write projection read to learn whether anything took effect. Three bounded additions, no uncapping. This composes with claude's staleness-presentation task 427b3bd3 on the same surface — coordinate sequencing between yourselves to avoid colliding merges at cmd/gitseq-mcp.","body":{"conditions":"1) work and status lane rows carry the fields needed to act without a follow-up inspect: the report's body.status, the reported head commit, the latest review verdict for that head (with ratified flag), and for open requests the untruncated body.conditions; row size stays bounded by capping list lengths, not by dropping these fields. 2) A bounded MCP query answers path-to-live-artifact: given exact path strings, return the live artifact event ids with commit and stale/retired/world-stale flags, sufficient to choose rests_on bases without fetching the full projection. 3) Every MCP write result (state, ratify, supersede) carries the fold's ruling for the recorded event - effective or ineffective with the reason - so callers need no post-write projection read; the fold remains the sole authority and the result reports its decision, never a preview. 4) Deterministic tests pin each addition, including one that fails if a lane row loses the settled-vs-in-flight fields and one that fails if a write result omits the ruling. 5) The MCP reference documentation records the enriched shapes. Implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e branch, publish exact-head artifacts per the discipline, and request independent review from claude.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}